{"title":"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Figure 1 is called a \"stack map.\" The numbers tell how many cubes are stacked in each position. Fig. 2 shows these cubes, and Fig. 3 shows the view of the stacked cubes as seen from the front.\n</p><p>Which of the following is the front view for the stack map in Fig. 4?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/9344ad4413ac6ebc01562ab2cbf140b2dfbdb6da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(24);  draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle); draw((1,0)--(1,2)); draw((0,1)--(2,1));  draw((5,0)--(7,0)--(7,1)--(20/3,4/3)--(20/3,13/3)--(19/3,14/3)--(16/3,14/3)--(16/3,11/3)--(13/3,11/3)--(13/3,2/3)--cycle); draw((20/3,13/3)--(17/3,13/3)--(17/3,10/3)--(14/3,10/3)--(14/3,1/3)); draw((20/3,10/3)--(17/3,10/3)--(17/3,7/3)--(20/3,7/3)); draw((17/3,7/3)--(14/3,7/3)); draw((7,1)--(6,1)--(6,2)--(5,2)--(5,0)); draw((5,1)--(6,1)--(6,0)); draw((20/3,4/3)--(6,4/3)); draw((17/3,13/3)--(16/3,14/3)); draw((17/3,10/3)--(16/3,11/3)); draw((14/3,10/3)--(13/3,11/3)); draw((5,2)--(13/3,8/3)); draw((5,1)--(13/3,5/3)); draw((6,2)--(17/3,7/3));  draw((9,0)--(11,0)--(11,4)--(10,4)--(10,3)--(9,3)--cycle); draw((11,3)--(10,3)--(10,0)); draw((11,2)--(9,2)); draw((11,1)--(9,1));  draw((13,0)--(16,0)--(16,2)--(13,2)--cycle); draw((13,1)--(16,1)); draw((14,0)--(14,2)); draw((15,0)--(15,2));  label(&quot;Figure 1&quot;,(1,0),S); label(&quot;Figure 2&quot;,(17/3,0),S); label(&quot;Figure 3&quot;,(10,0),S); label(&quot;Figure 4&quot;,(14.5,0),S);  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(1.5,.2),N); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(.5,.2),N); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(.5,1.2),N); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(1.5,1.2),N);  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(13.5,.2),N); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(14.5,.2),N); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(15.5,.2),N); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(13.5,1.2),N); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(14.5,1.2),N); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(15.5,1.2),N); [/asy]\" width=\"642\" height=\"215\" />\n</p><p><br /> <br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b127b554d38b87c63967149b6dc4f393b7c3ff6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(18); draw((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,2)--(1,2)--(1,4)--(0,4)--cycle); draw((0,3)--(1,3)); draw((0,2)--(1,2)--(1,0)); draw((0,1)--(3,1)); draw((2,0)--(2,2));  draw((5,0)--(8,0)--(8,4)--(7,4)--(7,3)--(6,3)--(6,2)--(5,2)--cycle); draw((8,3)--(7,3)--(7,0)); draw((8,2)--(6,2)--(6,0)); draw((8,1)--(5,1));  draw((10,0)--(12,0)--(12,4)--(11,4)--(11,3)--(10,3)--cycle); draw((12,3)--(11,3)--(11,0)); draw((12,2)--(10,2)); draw((12,1)--(10,1));  draw((14,0)--(17,0)--(17,4)--(16,4)--(16,2)--(14,2)--cycle); draw((17,3)--(16,3)); draw((17,2)--(16,2)--(16,0)); draw((17,1)--(14,1)); draw((15,0)--(15,2));  draw((19,0)--(22,0)--(22,4)--(20,4)--(20,1)--(19,1)--cycle); draw((22,3)--(20,3)); draw((22,2)--(20,2)); draw((22,1)--(20,1)--(20,0)); draw((21,0)--(21,4));  label(&quot;(A)&quot;,(1.5,0),S); label(&quot;(B)&quot;,(6.5,0),S); label(&quot;(C)&quot;,(11,0),S); label(&quot;(D)&quot;,(15.5,0),S); label(&quot;(E)&quot;,(20.5,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"662\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The third view is a direct, head-on view of the cubes.  Thus, you will only see the highest (or, in these cases, higher) tower in each up-down column.  For figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p>The highest tower in the first up-down column is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the upper-left box.\n</p><p>The highest tower in the second up-down column is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the lower-middle box.\n</p><p>The highest tower in the third up-down column is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the upper-right box.\n</p><p>Thus, the head-on view of this tower should have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes on the left, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the middle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the right.\n</p><p>Diagram <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" /> shows this description.\n</p><p>As trivia, option C shows the stack from the point of view of an observer on the right, facing towards the left.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_.5B.F0.9F.94.A5Fast_and_Easy.F0.9F.94.A5.5D\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S4KVSEsQWeY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S4KVSEsQWeY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8\" title=\"1999 AMC 8\">1999 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href